Size the activity bar overflow from the DOM instead of a cached dimension.

The mobile stylesheet hides the Manage section, which frees vertical space that
this.dimension was measured before. The overflow calculation then moves icons
into the "..." menu while the room for them is visibly there — on a phone, where
the bar is short to begin with, that is most of them.

Read through document.querySelector rather than a field because this class is
handed its container by a caller that does not retain it, and falls back to the
cached value when the element is not found, so nothing changes on layouts where
the query does not match.

